Scenario A: bulk pipeline
==============================================================================
    20 test images in experiments/scratch/demo (~2 MB each). img-008.png is 2 MB of random bytes, not an image.

--- 1. Pipeline (A Decision 3): validated at save, stored as an immutable version
    a pipeline with sigma=999 -> 400 {"code":"invalid_input","message":"input: filter 'blur': param 'sigma' must be in [0.3, 50]"}
    pipeline pipe_4b2b4b05e552 v1: grayscale -> fail-inject(img-007) -> resize(800)

--- 2. Batch + presigned POST uploads (A Decision 1): zero image bytes through the API
    20/20 uploaded straight to S3 in 30635 ms (each URL carries a signed content-length-range policy)

--- 3. Submit (Fact 9: S3 does not notify; we list and reconcile), then the Distributed Map runs
    202: run run_a52fb3405002, parent execution started; every image is its own child execution
